cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OffshoreForge in research or teaching, please cite it as below. Results
  depend on the bundled datasets; their SHA-256 hashes are pinned in
  backend/data_manifest.json, and the validation evidence (docs/engineering-audit-2026-10.md,
  the in-app Evidence page) is regenerated from the tests.
title: "OffshoreForge: an offshore wind engineering training and analysis platform"
abstract: >-
  Lifecycle-coupled engineering platform built around the SB-510 reference case
  (510 MW, 34 × IEA-15-240-RWT, 66 kV array, 2 × 108 km 220 kV HVAC export): wind
  resource and wake-based AEP, load flow, IEC 60909 short circuit, IEC 60287 cable rating,
  harmonics and converter–network stability, FRT, EMT energisation, IEC 61850 SCADA,
  forecasting, commissioning, support-structure dynamics, tower fatigue and fleet O&M,
  each checked against published references, standards or closed-form results.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Polat
    given-names: Mustafa
repository-code: "https://github.com/polat-mustafa/offshoreforge"
license: MIT
